From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:27:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop repeated deterministic tool input failures

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Stop retries of repeated typed input errors
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-fix
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0002-candidate-add-hook-context-and-post-tool-transform.patch

Patch intent:
Stop a turn after three matching typed deterministic tool-input failures,
including nested batch dispatches, in both turn loops. Unknown tool names use
the same typed classification; other untyped tool errors are not classified.

Why it exists:
Repeated invalid inputs can otherwise trigger repeated provider requests without
progress. Classification is explicit through a typed error, not inferred from
error text. This does not classify arbitrary validation or runtime failures.

Upstream integration points:
The change adds tool::retry_guard and wraps Registry::execute dispatches,
including nested BatchTool calls. Agent::run_turn and
Agent::run_turn_streaming_mpsc reset and check the shared per-turn guard. The
retry guard also depends on hook context established by patch 0002.

Update guidance:
Keep failure classification limited to explicit typed input errors and unknown
tool names. Preserve separate guard state for cloned registries, nested batch
dispatch tracking, the bounded repeat window, and terminal checks in both turn
loops. Preserve the hook context dependency inherited from patch 0002.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core retry_guard --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core malformed_tool_call_recovery_tests --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core tool::batch_tests --lib

